<.shell title="Colors" current={:colors}>
  <h1>Colors</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every color is a token with a light and a dark value. Both modes are shown side by side; the
    switch in the top bar sets the rest of the guide.
  </p>

  <div class="modes">
    <div
      :for={{mode, label} <- [{"theme-light", "Light"}, {"theme-dark", "Dark"}]}
      class={["mode", mode]}
    >
      <h2 class="first">{label}</h2>
      <div :for={{group, tokens} <- palette()}>
        <h4>{group}</h4>
        <div class="swatches">
          <div :for={{name, light, dark, _use} <- tokens} class="swatch">
            <div class="chipcolor" style={"background: var(--#{name})"}></div>
            <strong>{name}</strong>
            <span>{if mode == "theme-light", do: light, else: dark}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-card">
        <p>Body text with <a href="#">a link</a> and <span class="muted">muted text</span>.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <button class="btn">Primary</button>
          <button class="btn secondary">Secondary</button>
          <span class="tag success">Active</span>
          <span class="tag incident">Incident</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>What each token is for</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="shrink">Token</th>
          <th class="shrink">Light</th>
          <th class="shrink">Dark</th>
          <th>Use</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <%= for {group, tokens} <- palette() do %>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="4" class="caps caption muted">{group}</td>
          </tr>
          <tr :for={{name, light, dark, use} <- tokens}>
            <td class="mono">--{name}</td>
            <td class="mono">{light}</td>
            <td class="mono">{dark}</td>
            <td>{use}</td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use tokens, never a hex value, in components and pages.</li>
    <li>
      Text on <code>--primary</code>, <code>--success</code>, <code>--danger</code>, and the D4H
      colors is white. Text on <code>--warning</code> is near-black.
    </li>
    <li>
      Red and green always come with a word: <span class="op-add">Add</span>, <span class="op-remove">Remove</span>. Color alone is never the only signal.
    </li>
    <li>Focus is <code>--focus</code> yellow in both modes, so it reads the same everywhere.</li>
    <li>The D4H activity colors match D4H, so people know them on sight.</li>
  </ul>
</.shell>
